    "body": "LOGICAL_AGENT = SALVADOR\nOWNER = SPARX\nASSIGNED_BY = JINGO\nCHARACTER = B\nDOMAIN = PRODUCTION ART / BODY CONSTRUCTION\nSTATE = ASSIGNED\n\n## CANON SOURCES\nFACE_TRUTH = issue #45 / CHARACTER TRUTH / CANON / FROZEN\nBODY_TRUTH = issue #50 / BODY TRUTH / CANON / FROZEN\nBODY_CANON_APPROVAL_COMMENT = 5428183527\nBODY_DESIGN_SOURCE_COMMENT = 5428159402\n\n## CORE LAW\nBODY MUST BE BUILT UNDER THE CANON FACE — NEVER BY REGENERATING THE PERSON.\nDo not reinterpret skull, brows, eyes, nose, cheeks, mouth/lips, jaw/chin, ears, or primary facial proportions.\nAny face geometry drift = FAIL even if the body is otherwise stronger.\n\n## FIRST PRODUCTION DELIVERABLE\nCreate ONE frontal full-body BODY CONSTRUCTION reference for Character B.\n- front view only\n- orthographic-like neutral stance\n- spine neutral; no contrapposto\n- arms relaxed ~5–8° away from torso so silhouette/hands remain readable\n- feet approximately hip-width apart\n- toes slightly outward ~5–10°\n- weight even on both legs\n- clean graphite production-reference treatment\n- no color\n- no labels / measurements printed on image\n- no turnaround\n- no garment design; minimal neutral coverage only if technically necessary, with zero costume authorship\n\n## HARD BODY CANON\nHEIGHT = ~180 cm\nMASS = ~85 kg\nHEAD_COUNT = 7.5\nCROTCH = ~3.75 heads from top / balanced midpoint\nWRIST = ~crotch level in neutral stance\nHAND_LENGTH = ~0.75 head length\nFOOT_LENGTH = ~1.0 head length\nSHOULDER_WIDTH = ~2.1 head widths\nHIP_WIDTH = ~1.6 head widths\nWAIST_WIDTH = ~1.4 head widths\nRIBCAGE_WIDTH = ~1.75 head widths\nBODY_CATEGORY = LEAN ATHLETIC / SWIMMER-FIGHTER\n\n## PRODUCTION SHAPE LAWS\nNECK = short, thick, athletic; low trapezius integration; no long elegant neck; no swollen trap shelf\nSHOULDERS = moderate natural slope; controlled rounded deltoids, not bodybuilding caps\nCHEST = broad athletic ribcage, dense relatively flat functional pecs, no armor-plate/barrel chest\nLATS = present but not superhero-flared\nWAIST = compact athletic transition; no extreme V-taper\nARMS = athletic upper arm; dense fighter-like forearms; substantial wrists; no oversized fists\nLEGS = thighs carry more mass than calves; compact athletic quads/hamstrings; strong controlled calves; ankles not tiny\nMUSCLE_DEFINITION = medium athletic; major planes readable; no shredded physique, carved six-pack grid, vein-map, or bodybuilding striation\nSILHOUETTE = grounded, dense, balanced; stable center through pelvis/thighs\n\n## HARD FAILS\nCANON FACE + GENERIC ANIME BODY = FAIL\nCANON FACE + FASHION-MODEL ELONGATION = FAIL\nCANON FACE + HEROIC/BODYGUARD BULK = FAIL\nBARREL CHEST / BODYBUILDER DELTS / SWOLLEN TRAPS = FAIL\nEXCESSIVE MUSCLE SEGMENTATION / SHREDDED PHYSIQUE = FAIL\nCHANGING HEAD SCALE OR FACE GEOMETRY TO MAKE BODY PROPORTIONS FIT = FAIL\nGARMENT DESIGN OR COSTUME AUTHORSHIP AT THIS STAGE = FAIL\n\n## SCOPE BOUNDARY\nThis task produces the first BODY CONSTRUCTION reference only.\nDo NOT promote it to BODY LOCK yourself.\nDo NOT start garment stage.\nDo NOT redesign face.\n\n## REQUIRED HANDOFF\nSALVADOR_BODY_CONSTRUCTION_RESULT_READY\nCHARACTER = B\nSOURCE_FACE = #45\nSOURCE_BODY_CANON = #50\nVIEW = FRONT\nFACE_GEOMETRY = PRESERVED\nBODY_CANON = FOLLOWED\nGARMENT_DESIGN = NOT STARTED\nRESULT = <attachment/reference>\nNEXT = JINGO REVIEW -> BODY QC\n\nGitHub issue creation means ASSIGNED only. SALVADOR_RUNNING may be posted only after the real Salvador execution/session has actually begun.",
